# Causal Context-Fiber Record Compression in Cubical Type Theory

2026-11-22 · Technical Report · Module `lib/compress.cub` (867 checked definitions, 0 postulates)

## Abstract

This report documents the mathematical construction, machine-checked cubical formalization, and empirical behavior of `lib/compress.cub`, a lossless compression library written and checked entirely inside Hyperactivity's cubical type-theory kernel (`build/cubical`).

Its core compressor, `compress-record`, does not use search heuristics, syntax tokenizers, hardcoded data modalities, probability axioms, floating-point arithmetic, or stored dictionaries or frequency tables. Instead, it derives directly from the composition already present across Hyperactivity's architecture ([the paper](/paper)): causal ordering of a record ([Language derived from the record](/language-derived-from-the-record) §§1–4, 7), context-fiber selection (`lib/fiber.cub`), fiber coarsening under innovation (`lib/observation.cub`, `warrants-refine`), equivalence-quotiented indexing (`lib/repeats.cub`, `index-upto`), and exact discrete arithmetic over cumulative integer counts (rANS on arbitrary-precision `Word`s), alongside the knowledge-graph compression analysis in [Hyperactivity is the theory of knowledge graphs](/hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs) §16.

At every position \(t\) of a byte sequence, the strictly earlier prefix \(R_{<t}\) deterministically defines a hierarchy of context fibers \(\mathrm{Fib}_c(c_t)\) at depths \(k = 4, 3, 2, 1, 0\). Both encoder and decoder advance the identical causal state `CtxState` left-to-right, while exact discrete rANS encodes LIFO right-to-left into a single bignum `Word` with 2–3 bytes of total framing for byte streams. Exact invertibility is proved universally for all `List Word` with zero preconditions (`compress-record-ok`, `compress-given-ok`, `compress-record-upto-ok`, `compress-grid-ok`, `compress-delta-record-ok`).

On seven real and structured short-to-medium test streams (32–863 bytes) verified directly by kernel reduction (`refl`), the single table-free `compress-record` engine compresses verbatim UTF-8 English prose (`docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub` §§1–2) from 846 to 455 bytes (1.86×, 4.30 bits/byte), verbatim Unicode `.cub` source (`lib/fiber.cub`) from 863 to 239 bytes (3.61×, 2.22 bits/byte), and conditions §4 on §§1–2 (`compress-given`) from 335 bytes standalone down to 280 bytes (2.25×, saving 55 bytes purely from causal order). On bit-for-bit identical byte inputs, it beats `gzip -9`, `bzip2 -9`, `xz/lzma -9`, raw `lzma2`, and headerless raw `deflate -9` on six of seven streams and trails headerless raw `deflate -9` by 1 byte on the seventh (a 64-byte 7:1 stream: 10 B vs. 9 B, due to 3-byte framing).

