## 7. Honest Limitations, Cost Accounting, and Next Engineering Steps

No compression system is honestly understood without stating where it breaks down today. The exact limits of `lib/compress.cub` v2 are:

1. **Bignum rANS state growth (\(O(N^2)\) arithmetic without streaming renormalization).** `cf-enc-list` accumulates the entire compressed stream into a single arbitrary-precision `Word` before `word-to-bytes-go` unpacks it to bytes. For an \(N\)-byte input, intermediate `Word`s reach \(\Theta(N)\) bytes, so \(N\) rANS multiplications/divisions cost \(\Theta(N^2)\) word operations. That is fast at \(N \le 1\text{ KB}\) (863 B code compresses in ~5 seconds inside the unoptimized interaction-net evaluator; 14.86 s for the entire 867-definition file), but it will not scale to megabyte files until bounded-window streaming rANS renormalization (emitting/consuming 8-bit or 16-bit limbs when `s` leaves \([L, bL)\)) is proved and plugged in.
2. **Fixed context depth (\(k \le 4\)) and unbalanced `CtxTree`s.** Context depths 0–4 capture local morphology, syntax, and short phrases strongly on 32–1000 B streams, but on large files they miss long-range exact matches (e.g., repeated 40-byte identifiers or paragraphs) that LZMA and unbounded-order PPM* exploit. Moreover, `CtxTree` is currently an unbalanced BST whose worst-case lookup is \(O(\text{distinct contexts})\). Connecting `cstate-fiber-at` to the proved suffix-array / LCP / order-statistic index already in `lib/suffix-index.cub` (`si-index-ok`, `si-kth-ok`) will provide unbounded-depth exact fiber selection (`Infini-gram`-style longest-match fibers) in logarithmic lookup depth.
3. **Short-to-medium benchmark regime only.** None of the 7 kernel-checked witnesses exceeds 863 bytes. Measuring `compress-record` (once streaming renormalization and balanced/suffix-indexed fibers land) on standard large benchmarks (Calgary, Canterbury, Silesia, enwik8) is required before making any claims about large-corpus compression ratios relative to `zstd`, `lzma`, or `paq`/`cmix`.
4. **Relation to classical literature.** The algorithmic core is closely related to PPMD with exclusion (Cleary & Witten 1984; Moffat 1990) and exact integer rANS (Duda 2009, 2013). What is distinct here is not a claim of inventing context modeling or ANS from scratch, but: (a) deriving the exact zero-search, zero-table, quotient-parameterized, earliest-content mechanism natively from Hyperactivity's ordered-record and fiber semantics without probability axioms; (b) proving universal, zero-precondition lossless invertibility inside a cubical proof assistant with zero postulates; and (c) executing the proved code directly inside the kernel on real unedited prose and source code at competitive-to-superior ratios against industrial compressors in the short-to-medium regime.
5. **Automatic equivalence induction.** `compress-record-upto` currently accepts any caller-supplied quotient `q : Word → Word`. Closing the loop with automatic equivalence discovery — lifting distributional context-class induction (`induce-ctx-classes` in Section 3) and structural/univalent equivalences (`ua(e)`) online without search heuristics — remains open work.

